def on_page(c, doc):
    c.saveState(); c.setFont("DVS", 7.8); c.setFillColor(MUTED)
    c.drawString(doc.leftMargin, 0.42*inch, "The Doom Slayer  ·  D&D 5th Edition build (2024 rules; the Divinity Machine, the arsenal and the Slayer's own tricks are homebrew)")
    c.drawRightString(letter[0]-doc.rightMargin, 0.42*inch, f"page {doc.page}"); c.restoreState()
doc = SimpleDocTemplate("../pdf/Doom_Slayer_5e_Build.pdf", pagesize=letter, leftMargin=0.6*inch, rightMargin=0.6*inch, topMargin=0.6*inch, bottomMargin=0.7*inch, title="The Doom Slayer — D&D 5e Build", author="Claude")
W = letter[0] - 1.2*inch; S = []
S.append(P("The Doom Slayer", title))
S.append(P("Human (rebuilt) · Barbarian (Path of the Zealot) 14 / Fighter (Champion) 6 · Soldier · the Praetor Suit, the arsenal, and the Crucible", subtitle))
S.append(HRFlowable(width="100%", thickness=1.4, color=GREEN, spaceBefore=4, spaceAfter=8))
S.append(P("Built on the 2024 rules, canon-first like the Guy sheet: the numbers are sized to what he does on the page and in the game, with notes for a DM who wants to turn them down. Sources: Doom, Doom II and Doom 64 for the marine; the codex of Doom (2016) and Doom Eternal with both Ancient Gods parts for the Slayer; Doom: The Dark Ages and its Revelations expansion for the Sentinel years, which are the newest material and the earliest in his life."))
S.append(P("<b>Design calls.</b> He is a soldier who became something else: Fighter first for the marine (Archery for the guns, Action Surge, Champion crits, two attacks), then Barbarian because the thing the demons could not do is kill him. Rage is the Praetor Suit drinking damage; Reckless Attack is the only way he has ever fought; Relentless Rage and the Zealot's Rage Beyond Death are the Slayer's Testament, unbroken and unbent. The Divinity Machine sets Strength and Constitution past the human ceiling, the way Smasher's frame does. The Zealot's radiant fury is Argent energy. He does not speak, so his Charisma is what it is."))
S.append(P("Snapshot: the Ancient Gods, level 20 (Barbarian 14 / Fighter 6)", h2)); S.append(rule())
block = [P("The Doom Slayer", statname),
 P("Medium Humanoid (Human, remade by the Divinity Machine), age unknown · the Praetor Suit, the Super Shotgun, the Crucible on his back, the Sentinel Hammer · the italics are a raging Slayer, which is the only kind in a fight", stattag),
 P("<b>AC</b> 20 (Praetor Suit) · <b>HP</b> 298, plus 60 Argent shielding at the start of every fight · <b>Speed</b> 40 ft (Fast Movement), 50 with Speedy's Dash, double jump and climb (Athlete) · <b>Initiative</b> +4 with advantage · <b>Proficiency</b> +6", stat),
 abil_table(["24 (+7)","18 (+4)","22 (+6)","8 (−1)","12 (+1)","8 (−1)"], W-24), Spacer(1,4),
 P("<b>Saves</b> Str +13, Con +12; advantage on Dex saves (Danger Sense) and on saves against being Frightened or Charmed (the Divinity Machine); Fanatical Focus rerolls one failed save per Rage at +3 · <b>Skills</b> Athletics +13 (advantage), Intimidation +5 (Strength-based while raging), Perception +7, Survival +7 · <b>Save DC</b> for his gear 18 (Dex-based) or 21 (Strength-based)", stat),
 P("<b>Defenses.</b> Rage: resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing; the Suit adds resistance to fire and radiant. Shield Saw parry: a reaction takes 1d10+13 off one attack, and if that empties it the attacker is staggered (no reactions until its next turn). Relentless Rage at 0 HP: DC 10 Con, back to 28. <i>Rage Beyond Death: at 0 HP while raging he keeps acting; he makes death saves, and dies only on the third failure or when the Rage ends with him still at 0.</i> Immune to disease and aging.", stat),
 P("<b>Attacks</b> (two per Attack action; Action Surge once a fight). Guns use Dexterity with Archery: +12. Melee uses Strength: +13, <i>+3 damage raging</i>. Crits on 19–20. Savage Attacker rerolls one weapon's dice a turn. <i>Divine Fury: the first hit of each turn deals +1d6+7 radiant, the Argent in the blow.</i> Sharpshooter: no penalty at long range or point-blank.", stat),
 bullets(["<b>Super Shotgun</b> +12, 4d8 piercing, both barrels, range 20/60, Push. <b>Meat Hook:</b> bonus action, pull himself to within 5 ft of a creature within 60 ft without provoking.",
          "<b>Ballista</b> +12, 3d10 force, 150/600, Slow. <b>Destroyer Blade</b> (recharge 5–6): a 60-ft line, Dex DC 18, 8d10 force, half on a save. <b>Heavy Cannon</b> +12, 2d10 piercing, 120/480. <b>Plasma Rifle</b> +12, 2d8 lightning; <b>Heat Blast</b> (bonus, recharge 3): 15-ft cone, 4d8 fire. <b>Rocket Launcher:</b> 10-ft radius within 120 ft, Dex DC 18, 6d8 fire, half on a save. <b>Chaingun</b> +12, 2d8 piercing, or a 10-ft cube at DC 18.",
          "<b>Unmakyr</b> (3 charges): three bolts at +12 for 3d8 force each, in a cone. <b>BFG-9000</b> (3 charges): an action, a 120-ft line 20 ft wide; every creature in the line or within 20 ft of it makes a Dex save DC 18, taking 20d10 force on a failure, half on a success.",
          "<b>The Crucible</b> (3 charges): +13, 12d12+7 slashing that ignores resistance and immunity, and if the target has 150 hit points or fewer afterward it is cut in half and dies. Argent cuts anything; it cut the Titan, the Khan Maykr, the Icon of Sin and the Dark Lord. <b>Chainsaw</b> (3 fuel): a creature with 60 HP or fewer is cut in half; otherwise +13, 4d8 slashing. <b>Doomblade / bare hands:</b> +13, 1d8+7, and a creature at 15% or less of its hit points is Glory Killed on a hit.",
          "<b>Blood Punch</b> (2 charges, one back per Glory Kill): replaces an attack, a 10-ft cone, 8d10+7 bludgeoning, Str DC 21 or knocked prone. <b>Sentinel Hammer</b> (1 charge, back per Glory Kill): an action, every creature within 15 ft takes 6d10 force and makes a Con save DC 19 or is Stunned until the end of its next turn.",
          "<b>Flame Belch</b> (bonus, recharge 3): 15-ft cone, 2d6 fire and Burning (1d6 a turn); +10 Argent shielding per creature set alight. <b>Ice Bomb</b> (bonus, recharge 4): 15-ft radius, Dex DC 18 or frozen until the end of his next turn (Restrained and Incapacitated; attacks against it have advantage and melee hits are critical hits). <b>Frag Grenade</b> (bonus, recharge 3): 10-ft radius, Dex DC 18, 6d6, half on a save.",
          "<b>Shield Saw</b> (Dark Ages): thrown +12, 3d10 slashing, up to three creatures in a 30-ft line, and it comes back. <b>Shield Charge:</b> a 30-ft straight line; each creature in it makes a Str save DC 21 or takes 3d10 and falls prone. <b>Chain Spear</b> (Revelations): +13, 2d10+7 piercing, reach 10 ft, thrown 30/90 and recalled; a hit can drag a Large or smaller creature 15 ft. Mace, flail and the power gauntlet are martial melee at +13 with Topple, Push and Sap."]),
 P("<b>Rip and Tear.</b> When he reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack, the chainsaw or the Crucible, he regains 4d10 hit points, 20 Argent shielding, and a charge of Blood Punch and the Hammer. <b>Dash:</b> two charges, one back each turn: a bonus action to move 20 ft without provoking, or a reaction when a ranged attack or area effect targets him to move 20 ft first and give the attack disadvantage or himself advantage on the save. <b>The Slayer's Fear:</b> a fiend that sees him makes a Wisdom save DC 18 at the start of its turn or is Frightened of him; the demons called him the Hellwalker for a reason.", stat),
 P("<b>Resources.</b> Rage ×5 (+3 damage, 10 minutes), Action Surge ×1, Second Wind ×3 (1d10+6), Brutal Strike (+2d10 and a shove or a hamstring; Improved: two effects), Relentless Rage, Warrior of the Gods (a pool of healing d12s equal to his Barbarian level), Zealous Presence (a roar: allies gain advantage), Weapon Mastery ×4, Heroic Inspiration each long rest. <b>Feats</b> Savage Attacker, Tough, Sharpshooter, Great Weapon Master, Grappler, Athlete, Speedy.", stat),
 P("<b>How he fights.</b> Rage on the way in, Reckless Attack every turn, Meat Hook to close. The BFG opens any fight that matters and he has three of them; the Crucible ends anything that is already hurt. Ice Bomb, then a melee hit that crits; Flame Belch for shielding; Glory Kills for health. He does not take cover, does not retreat, and does not stop. If something takes him to 0, it finds out why the demons buried him instead.", stat)]
box = Table([[f] for f in block], colWidths=[W]); box.setStyle(TableStyle([("BACKGROUND",(0,0),(-1,-1),PARCH),("BOX",(0,0),(-1,-1),1.0,GREEN),("LEFTPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),11),("RIGHTPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),11),("TOPPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),1),("BOTTOMPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),1),("TOPPADDING",(0,0),(-1,0),9),("BOTTOMPADDING",(0,-1),(-1,-1),9)])); S.append(box)
S.append(P("Homebrew, and why each number", h2)); S.append(rule())
hb = [("The Divinity Machine", "bloodline-style feature, gained at Barbarian 3 (the Seraphim's gift)", "His Strength becomes 24 and his Constitution 22. He no longer ages and cannot catch a disease, and he has advantage on saves against being Frightened or Charmed. The Seraphim put a marine in the machine and a Slayer walked out; this is the sheet's version of that, and it is the same tool Smasher's frame uses."),
 ("The Praetor Suit", "legendary; Sentinel armor remade by the Wretch", "AC 18 + Dex (max 2). It counts as medium armor, so he can Rage in it. Argent shielding: 60 temporary hit points at the start of a fight, refilled by Flame Belch (+10 a creature) and Glory Kills (+20). Resistance to fire and radiant. The suit holds every weapon he owns and never runs out of anything but BFG cells."),
 ("The Crucible", "3 charges, back on a long rest", "An Argent blade that cuts anything. The numbers: 12d12+7 (about 85) that no resistance or immunity touches, and a cut-in-half clause at 150 hit points, because in the games a charge kills any non-boss outright and finishes bosses once they are broken. That is the Titan (the Slayer's codex), the Khan Maykr, the Icon of Sin (armor stripped, then the blade in the brain) and the Dark Lord."),
 ("The BFG-9000", "3 charges", "The game's answer to a room. 20d10 is a Meteor Swarm concentrated into a line, three times a day, which is what three BFG cells are. Bosses in the game shrug it off; a DM can give any creature with Legendary Resistance resistance to it."),
 ("Rage Beyond Death", "the 2014 Zealot's level-14 feature, used instead of the 2024 Rage of the Gods", "At 0 hit points while raging he keeps acting, makes death saves, and dies only on the third failure or if the Rage ends. The 2024 feature gives flight and a reaction revive; this one is the Slayer's Testament: they could not kill him, only bury him."),
 ("Glory Kills, Blood Punch, the Hammer", "the Eternal loop", "Health from melee kills, Argent from fire, charges from executions. The 15% Glory Kill clause is the game's stagger. The Hammer is the Ancient Gods Part Two weapon that stuns everything around him."),
 ("The Shield Saw, Chain Spear, mace, flail, gauntlet", "the Dark Ages and Revelations kit", "He is an iron tank in the Dark Ages, and the shield is the whole game: a parry that staggers, a thrown buzzsaw, a charge. Keep them on the sheet for the Sentinel-era snapshot; the Eternal-era Slayer carries the Super Shotgun instead."),
 ("What 5e cannot copy", "", "Thirty seconds of a fight at the speed he fights it. The Atlan, a mech the height of a city block, and Serrat, the cybernetic dragon, are vehicles: use them as the DM's set pieces, not his stat block.")]
